  "audit_notes": "Rule C. NDB 18402 canonical is present but two macros exceed the \u00b15% gate: Water +9.4% (build=21.55g vs canonical=19.7g) and Fiber \u221256.8% (build=1.47g vs canonical=3.4g). Fiber discrepancy is a USDA SR Legacy database anomaly \u2014 NDB 18402 reports 3.4g fiber/100g for the unbaked recipe while the identical baked recipe (NDB 18336) reports 1.7g fiber/100g; baking concentrates nutrients (yfw=0.38), so the baked version should have MORE fiber/100g than the unbaked version, not half as much. NDB 18402 Fiber=3.4 is physically implausible and consistent with a USDA measurement or transcription error. Water gap (+9.4%) is modest; raw dough water content varies with exact ice-water absorption. All other macros: Protein +0.4%, Fat \u22123.2%, Carb \u22121.9%, Energy \u22122.6% \u2014 all within \u00b15%. Ingredient quantities are identical to CRUST_002 (Rule A PASS); the only structural difference is no baking (yfw=1.0). Locked May 14 2026.",
